// A `break` written after a `ret` is never reached, and what the loop holds
// is as the `ret` left it, not given away.
//
// Ownership marked every binding a `ret` drops as moved, so a dead `break`
// after it left its loop with them all moved. A `for` around that loop then
// read its borrowed list as moved at the end of its body, and asked where it
// was moved, which nothing had recorded: the analysis panicked. Dead code
// reading what a `ret` drops was refused as a use after a move it is not.
fun first(l: [u8], s: string): u8
  for w in ref l
    loop
      debuglog s
      ret w
      debuglog s
      break
    end loop
  end for
  ret : u8 / 0
end fun
debuglog first([7, 8], "looped")
debuglog first([], "never")
